## Why This Is Asked

This question probes ability to design end-to-end scalable ingestion with strong isolation and cost discipline, plus onboarding automation.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation strategies (namespaces, resource groups)
- Ingestion options (IoT Hub vs Event Hubs) and scaling
- Data encryption with CMK and Key Vault
- RBAC, Service Principals, least privilege
- Onboarding automation (ARM/Bicep/Terraform), CI/CD
- Monitoring, auditing, budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo onboarding snippet (illustrative only)
async function onboardTenant(tenantId){
  await createEventHubNamespace(`tenant-${tenantId}-eh`);
  await createStorageAccount(`tenant${tenantId}sa`);
  await assignRBAC(tenantId, 'Contributor');
  await configureCMK(`tenant-${tenantId}-cmk`);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation boundaries at scale?
- What are the trade-offs of per-tenant storage vs a shared data lake with tagging?
